      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are correct that the humanitarian cost is a primary reason for the \"anti-sanctions\" movement, which argues that uninhibited power often leads to human rights abuses rather than democracy. In practice, this is frequently the \"colonial rationality\" where powerful states justify aggression as legitimate democracy promotion even when the results fail. Many scholars now argue that without a genuine moral imperative and clear adherence to international law, any \"sanctions\" are indeed a hypocritical tool for imperialism that often ends up hurting the very people it claims to save.",
